rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:87:- (1) **Busy state**: the pane exists and the agent/session match, but herdr is not `idle`/`done` or tmux is in copy-mode.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:105:- Group review cards use durable dispatch automatically. Explicit `--kind fix|sync|wrap-up`, `--dispatch-id`, or `--base <full-SHA>` selects it for working or non-group cards. Default kind is fix. Select wrap-up explicitly for post-integration completion. A new request without base uses the current working directory's Git HEAD.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:116:- Every bound author update carries the same ID/epoch and current expected revision. Bound review disposition JSON also carries `authorization: {"dispatch_id":"...","epoch":1}`; legacy records remain unchanged. Complete fix/sync with `move review`, or wrap-up with `move done --result completed`, carrying `--dispatch-id`, `--execution-epoch`, `--delivery-commit <final-full-SHA>` and an applicable `--disposition <card-relative-artifact>`. Completion and its receipt commit atomically. Existing done/review evidence gates still apply; a recorded SHA is not Git integration verification.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:124:- The optional `agents` configuration declares execution names, executable paths, pane process names, CLI dialects or argv templates, and session modes. Custom agents are execution-only; reviewer isolation and `*_REVIEW_BIN` remain independent.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:168:- The task file asks the agent to try to delete it when done; failure to delete or leftover files do not affect the result.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:186:- When the original agent is already dead, close only when the container topology can be proven; when the original address is empty, foreground/console, or the same as the new address, record N/A.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:196:- Both the override and the reverse lookup keep using `pane get` to verify that the pane exists, the agent and `agent_session.value` match exactly, and the existing pane state is `idle` or `done`.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:221:- herdr recovery liveness follows the new-pane criteria of `resume`, where the state still only accepts `idle`, `working`, `blocked` and rejects `done` and `unknown`.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:228:- `dismiss` only accepts `done/` or `archived/` cards and does not change the card body or state.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:235:- Before delivery, reuse the exact agent and session match of `notify`: herdr additionally requires `agent_status` to be `idle` or `done`; tmux additionally requires the pane to be alive, not in copy-mode, and with a matching foreground process.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:247:- `init` idempotently creates the board and the 7 state directories (`backlog`, `todo`, `working`, `review`, `done`, `archived`, `trash`); rerunning on an existing board only creates missing directories, and Git projects only update the local `info/exclude`.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:254:- Six launchers: `auto` is resolved at start time and the result is not written back to the configuration.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:255:- auto selection order: when inside herdr (`HERDR_ENV=1`), start with `herdr`; otherwise when inside tmux, start with `tmux`; when inside both, herdr wins; when inside neither, fail without claiming, and do not fall back to `tmux-session`, `foreground`, or `console`.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:266:- POSIX defaults to `auto`; Windows defaults to `console`.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:268:- The configuration likewise accepts `auto` on Windows, but there it only resolves to herdr; the options panel does not offer `auto`.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:285:- `check` by default checks invalid entries outside `done/` `archived/` and exits non-zero on errors.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:286:- For `todo/`, `working/`, `review/` cards, it also checks contract completeness: missing required sections, leftover `<FILL_IN>` placeholders, or acceptance criteria without `- [ ]` items all count as invalid.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:288:- When task IDs are given, only the targets and cross-state/cross-form conflicts are checked; unrelated invalid entries do not affect the result, and targets in `done/` or `archived/` are checked too.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:291:- By default, prerequisite cards in `done/` or `archived/` are only confirmed to exist; only `--all` checks them and their full reachable graph.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:316:- Group membership changes emit `membership-change`. Additions join immediately. Removals and ownership changes that remove a member from its former watched group (even if it remains in another watched group) carry `removed` and set `reconciliation_required: true` for the rest of the subscription. Do not infer satisfied dependencies from a shrinking set: re-check the contract, membership versions, and actual delivery first. An initially empty group and overlapping targets are rejected.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:317:- `membership_complete: true` and `read_status: committed` describe a complete observation, not authorization to release dependencies. Scan problems or unreadable ownership fail closed with a terminal `membership-unknown` event, `membership_complete: false`, `reconciliation_required: true`, and a nonzero exit. Task values on that event are the previous complete snapshot, or empty maps before any successful snapshot; never treat them as fresh complete facts. Explicit task-only watches use targeted reads; group expansion checks all possible members without probing unrelated agents.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:319:- `dispatches`, keyed by task ID, carries the current dispatch summary from the same shared-lock snapshot as card state/revision: `dispatch_id`, `task_id`, `kind`, `epoch`, `state`, dispatch `revision`, original intent `created_at`, the current epoch’s effective acceptance deadline `confirm_by`, `age_seconds`, and durable `accepted`/`completed` receipts with card revisions and applicable delivery/disposition references. `created_at` stays at the original intent creation time, and `age_seconds` is measured from it. Ordinary authority uses the intent’s deadline; a wrap-up-only grant uses its own independent deadline without rewriting the original intent. Message bodies are omitted. Unbound cards have no invented receipts. Older superseded IDs remain queryable with `dispatch show`; this is not a history list.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:320:- A same-refresh review-working-review/done round trip remains provable by its same-ID receipts in the next event or restart snapshot, including completion before notify returns. A completion receipt is not proof of Git integration or review closure.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:321:- `confirmation_pending` is true only for prepared/delivery-unknown; `confirmation_overdue` additionally means the current epoch’s effective acceptance deadline elapsed. Accepted work has no inferred completion deadline. The deadline wakes subscription independently of refresh/heartbeat and never resets on same-epoch retries, unrelated events, or subscription restart.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:322:- At expiry, including an already-expired initial snapshot, emit `dispatch-attention` with overdue task IDs in `attention`, current dispatch facts, available `liveness`, and `reconciliation_required=true`. Schedule a bounded probe; if a batch is active, retain one coalesced request until it joins. Further batch completions report still-overdue facts again; heartbeats continue probing. Alive is separate from missing business progress, with observation and dispatch ages reported separately. Attention never performs recovery, retry, card mutation or dependency release. Missing/corrupt dispatch evidence for a monitored card fails the read instead of being treated as absent.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:323:- Heartbeats remain independent of state, task-update, and membership events. When monitored `working/` or pending-dispatch `review/` cards exist, the heartbeat carries `liveness` items with `agent`, `status`, `channel`, and `detail`, reusing check's four-state classifier. Probe failures count as `unknown` and do not end the subscription; fast refreshes do not enqueue probes. Pending review cards with a prepared/delivery-unknown current dispatch also receive liveness; ordinary review and completed review cards do not. Without eligible cards, liveness is omitted.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:327:- Ctrl+C, supported platform termination signals and caller cancellation stop and join all owned probe/output work. No automatic exit occurs when all cards are done. File-system/kernel I/O and process reaping remain OS-dependent, not hard real-time guarantees.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:343:- Single click focuses or selects a card, double click opens details, drag-selected text is copied to the system clipboard automatically.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:345:- `/` or clicking the top-bar search area searches, `y` copies the task ID, Enter opens details, `a` toggles the archived column, `t` cycles auto/light/dark, `o` opens options, `?` opens the key overlay (any key closes it), `r` refreshes, `q` quits.
rules/KANDER-KANBAN-RULES.md:348:- `hjkl`/arrow keys move the cursor, the wheel scrolls, Ctrl-d/u half page, Ctrl-f/b or PgUp/PgDn full page, `gg`/`G` to top/bottom, `/` searches the body, `n`/`N` jump between matches, `v`/`V` character/line selection then `y` copies, and drag selection also copies automatically.
